1. Install Required Dependencies
Ensure you have lucide-react and tailwindcss installed in your project:
npm install lucide-react

2. Save the File
Place the generated code into your project's src folder as App.jsx (or ApiDashboard.jsx).	

3. Import into Your App Entrypoint
In your src/main.jsx (or src/index.js / src/App.js), import and render the component:

import React from 'react';
import ReactDOM from 'react-dom/client';
import App from './App'; // Import the dashboard component
import './index.css'; // Make sure Tailwind CSS directives are imported here

ReactDOM.createRoot(document.getElementById('root')).render(
  <React.StrictMode>
    <App />
  </React.StrictMode>
);

4. Ensure Tailwind CSS is Configured
If you haven't set up Tailwind CSS yet, ensure your src/index.css contains:
@tailwind base;
@tailwind components;
@tailwind utilities;

